              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "മണിക്കൂർ (maṇikkūr) — \"an hour\". It begins with മണി, the word in ഒരു മണി, \"one o'clock\"."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "മണിക്കൂർ (maṇikkūr) joins maṇi, \"hour, bell\" (DEDR 4672, with Tamil maṇi; DEDR asks whether it is Sanskrit maṇi, \"jewel\", CDIAL 9731), to native kūr, \"part, share, a division of time\" (DEDR 1924, with Tamil kūṟu)."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Sixty minutes."
